Provenance and onward obligations

These files are derived from a publicly available dataset that the authors
neither own nor collected:

  Anderson, Anthony (2024). Multi-Region Marketing Mix Modelling (MMM) Dataset
  for Several eCommerce Brands. figshare. Dataset, version 3.
  https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.25314841.v3

That dataset is itself released under CC BY 4.0. Reusing these files therefore
means crediting both this repository and the source dataset above.

Changes made to the source: the 143 source series were reduced to 142 candidates
by removing one series with a corrupt purchase spike, then screened to the 99 that
meet the history-length, completeness and media-spend-coverage bar described in
Section 3.2 of the paper; per-channel spend columns were summed into three totals
(Google, Meta, TikTok); and only the series and organisation identifiers, the
industry classification, the date, the target and the three spend totals were
retained. Everything in forecasts/ and results/ is new work computed from that
corpus.

Two further points:

1. The authors license only their own contribution: the qualification screen, the
   fitted forecasts and the derived metrics. Rights in the underlying source data
   remain with its original publisher under its own licence.

2. Organisation and series identifiers are the anonymised identifiers published
   in the source dataset; no organisation is named. We ask that users make no
   attempt to re-identify any organisation in it.
